  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations for Electrical Contractors and Other Wiring Installation Contractors (NAICS 238210) total $405M in FY2026 to date. There are 1,875 awards with an average award size of $216K. Obligations are down 48.8% year over year. Looking at the fiscal-year series, FY21 was $792M, FY22 was $853M, FY23 was $945M, FY24 was $824M, FY25 was $791M, and FY26 is $405M. Buying in FY2026 to date is concentrated: Department of Defense leads with $97.3M, followed by Department of Veterans Affairs at $94.2M and Department of State at $76.6M. Other notable agency buyers include Department of Transportation at $51.2M, Department of Homeland Security at $39.7M, and Department of Justice at $14.7M. Vendor concentration is apparent: XATOR LLC has $58.7M in obligations and SINTELA INC has $36.3M, while the top ten vendors include J & J MECHANICAL AND CONSTRUCTION GROUP LLC at $19.2M and JBW GROUP LLC at $8.2M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations fall year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 48.8% year over year to $405M in FY2026 to date. Recent fiscal years were higher, with FY23 at $945M, FY24 at $824M, and FY25 at $791M, showing a clear decline into the current fiscal-year total. This fiscal-year total reflects current-year activity through the date shown and is lower than multiple prior years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2026 buying?",
        "body": "Three agencies account for the largest shares: Department of Defense at $97.3M, Department of Veterans Affairs at $94.2M, and Department of State at $76.6M. On the vendor side, XATOR LLC leads with $58.7M and SINTELA INC follows with $36.3M, while the top ten vendors range down to JBW GROUP LLC at $8.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
